></path><path d=\"m22 7-8.5 8.5-5-5L2 17\"></path></svg>Salary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/tax-data\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#webpage\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator\",\"name\":\"Massachusetts Tax Calculator 2026\",\"description\":\"Free Massachusetts paycheck calculator with 5% flat state income tax and 9% surtax over $1M for 2026 take-home pay estimates.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-06-25\",\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#author\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#breadcrumb\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Massachusetts Tax Calculator\"}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#webapp\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Massachusetts Tax Calculator 2026\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"FinanceApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Web\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":0,\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator\"},\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#author\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#author\",\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much is Massachusetts state income tax in 2026?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Massachusetts has a flat 5% rate on most income, plus a 4% surtax (the millionaire's tax) on income exceeding $1 million — making the effective top rate 9%. For the vast majority of earners making under $1M, it's just 5%. That's lower than many progressive states' top rates but higher than flat-tax states like Pennsylvania (3.07%) or Indiana (3.05%).\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does Massachusetts have a standard deduction?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Nope. Massachusetts doesn't offer a standard deduction or personal exemption at the state level. Your entire gross income (minus any pre-tax deductions like 401(k) or HSA) is subject to the 5% rate. That's a drawback compared to states like Georgia or North Carolina that offer standard deductions.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the Massachusetts millionaire's tax?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Voters approved a 4% surtax on income above $1 million starting in 2023, bringing the effective rate to 9% on that portion. So if you earn $1.2M, the first $1M is taxed at 5% ($50,000) and the next $200K is taxed at 9% ($18,000). It only affects roughly 1% of Massachusetts taxpayers but generates significant revenue for education and transportation.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does Massachusetts tax Social Security benefits?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. Massachusetts does not tax Social Security benefits. However, most other retirement income — including 401(k) withdrawals, IRA distributions, and pensions — IS taxed at the 5% flat rate. That makes Massachusetts less retiree-friendly than states like Florida or Texas that have no income tax at all.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How does the overall tax burden in Massachusetts compare?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Massachusetts has a moderate-to-high overall tax burden. The 5% flat income tax is reasonable, but property taxes average 1.15%, the combined sales tax is 6.25% (state only — no local sales tax), and there's no standard deduction. On a $75K salary, you'd pay about $3,750 in state income tax, which is more than Indiana ($2,220 after exemptions) but less than California (around $4,100).\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is Massachusetts tax-friendly for retirees?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Not particularly. While Social Security is exempt, pensions, 401(k), and IRA withdrawals are all taxed at 5%. Property taxes are above average at 1.15%, and the cost of living in Massachusetts — especially housing near Boston — is among the highest in the country. Florida or New Hampshire (no income tax on wages) are better options for retirees in the region.\"}}]}]}</script><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\" aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">Massachusetts</span></nav><div class=\"mb-4 flex justify-center\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2 h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"19\" r=\"3\"></circle><line x1=\"8.59\" x2=\"15.42\" y1=\"13.51\" y2=\"17.49\"></line><line x1=\"15.41\" x2=\"8.59\" y1=\"6.51\" y2=\"10.49\"></line></svg>Share:</span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Massachusetts%20Tax%20Calculator%202026%20%7C%205%25%20Flat%20%26%209%25%20Surtax&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fthetaxcalc.com%2Fmassachusetts-tax-calculator&amp;via=TheTaxCalc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/30 p-2 transition-all hover:bg-sky-500/10 hover:text-sky-400 hover:border-sky-500/30\" aria-label=\"Share on Twitter / X\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-twitter h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M22 4s-.7 2.1-2 3.4c1.6 10-9.4 17.3-18 11.6 2.2.1 4.4-.6 6-2C3 15.5.5 9.6 3 5c2.2 2.6 5.6 4.1 9 4-.9-4.2 4-6.6 7-3.8 1.1 0 3-1.2 3-1.2z\"></path></svg></a><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthetaxcalc.com%2Fmassachusetts-tax-calculator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/30 p-2 transition-all hover:bg-blue-500/10 hover:text-blue-400 hover:border-blue-500/30\" aria-label=\"Share on LinkedIn\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-linkedin h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z\"></path><rect width=\"4\" height=\"12\" x=\"2\" y=\"9\"></rect><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2\"></circle></svg></a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"justify-center whitespace-nowrap font-medium disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:text-accent-foreground dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/30 px-3 py-2 text-xs transition-all hover:bg-muted/50\" aria-label=\"Copy link\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link2 lucide-link-2 h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M9 17H7A5 5 0 0 1 7 7h2\"></path><path d=\"M15 7h2a5 5 0 1 1 0 10h-2\"></path><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line></svg>Copy Link</button></div></div><div class=\"mb-8 text-center\"><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl\">Free Massachusetts Tax Calculator</h1><p class=\"mt-2 text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto\">Calculate your 2026 Massachusetts take-home pay after 5% flat state tax (9% surtax over $1M), federal tax &amp; FICA. No sign-up.</p><p class=\"mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Last reviewed: January 2026 · Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T &amp; state revenue departments</p></div><!--$!--><template data-dgst=\"BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING\"></template><div class=\"space-y-6\"><div class=\"grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-5\"><div class=\"space-y-4 lg:col-span-3\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-6 w-40 mb-4\"></div><div class=\"space-y-4\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-2/3\"></div></div></div></div><div class=\"lg:col-span-2\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-6 w-32 mb-4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-20 w-full mb-4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-3/4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-1/2\"></div></div></div></div></div><!--/$--><div id=\"scenario-comparison\" class=\"mt-8\"><div id=\"scenario-comparison\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><div data-state=\"closed\" data-slot=\"collapsible\"><div data-slot=\"card\" class=\"text-card-foreground flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border py-6 shadow-sm border-blue-500/20 bg-card/80 backdrop-blur-sm\"><div data-slot=\"collapsible-trigger\" class=\"@container/card-header grid auto-rows-min grid-rows-[auto_auto] items-start gap-1.5 px-6 has-data-[slot=card-action]:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] [.border-b]:pb-6 cursor-pointer pb-4 transition-colors hover:bg-muted/30\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_6av5uhtb_\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-state=\"closed\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-5 w-5 text-blue-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg><div data-slot=\"card-title\" class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Compare Tax Scenarios</div><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-accent [a&amp;]:hover:text-accent-foreground text-xs border-blue-500/30 text-blue-400\">New</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground transition-transform\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></div><div data-slot=\"card-description\" class=\"text-muted-foreground text-sm\">Compare up to 4 scenarios side by side — different states, 401(k) contributions, or filing statuses</div></div><div data-state=\"closed\" id=\"radix-_R_6av5uhtb_\" hidden=\"\" data-slot=\"collapsible-content\"></div></div></div></div></div><section class=\"mt-8 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3\">Related Tools &amp; Resources</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2\"><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><span>💵</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Paycheck Calculator</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Full take-home pay breakdown</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/new-york-tax-calculator\"><span>🏠</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">New York Calculator</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Compare NY 4%–10.9% vs MA 5%/9%</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/relocation-calculator\"><span>📊</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Relocation Calculator</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Compare MA to other states</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/salary\"><span>💰</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Salary After Tax</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Take-home pay at every level</p></div></a></div></section><div class=\"mt-12 space-y-10\"><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">How This Calculator Works</h2><div class=\"space-y-4\"><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Massachusetts charges a flat 5% income tax rate, with a 9% surtax on income over $1,000,000. For most earners, it's a straightforward 5% — no brackets to figure out. The state standard deduction is $4,400 (single) or $8,800 (married). On a $100,000 salary after the standard deduction, you'd pay about $4,780 in state tax. Simple enough.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The 9% surtax kicks in on taxable income above $1,000,000, making the effective top marginal rate 9% on that excess income. If you're earning seven figures in Massachusetts, that surtax is significant — it turns a $1.5M income into roughly $70,000 more in state tax compared to someone just under the threshold.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">On top of state tax, you've got federal progressive brackets with the standard deduction, plus FICA at 7.65% combined. <a href=\"/401k-retirement-calculator\">401(k) contributions</a> reduce taxable income at both the federal and state level, which is especially valuable here since Massachusetts doesn't allow many other state-level deductions.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Massachusetts doesn't tax Social Security benefits. Property taxes average about 1.23%, and the combined sales tax is 6.25% — one of the lower state sales tax rates. No local sales tax add-ons either. <a href=\"/relocation-calculator\">Compare MA to other states</a> to see if the tax picture works for you.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">How It&#x27;s Calculated</h2><div class=\"space-y-5\"><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Formula</h3><div class=\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\">MA State Tax = (Gross Income − MA Standard Deduction) × 5%, plus 9% surtax on income over $1M</div></div><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Step-by-Step</h3><ol class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">1</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Subtract MA standard deduction ($4,400 single / $8,800 married) from gross income</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">2</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Apply MA flat 5% rate to state taxable income</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">3</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">If income exceeds $1,000,000, apply 9% surtax on the excess (millionaire&#x27;s tax)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">4</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Add federal tax (10%–37% progressive brackets) and FICA (7.65%)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">5</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Sum all taxes and subtract from gross pay for net take-home</span></li></ol></div><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Example</h3><div class=\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">$100,000 salary, single in MA: MA taxable = $95,600. MA tax = $4,780. Federal ≈ $11,670. FICA = $7,650. Net ≈ $75,900.</div></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">For detailed data sources and full methodology, see our <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\" href=\"/methodology\">Methodology &amp; Data Sources</a> page.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Key Rates &amp; Data for 2026</h2><div class=\"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">MA Flat Tax Rate</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">5%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">MA Surtax (over $1M)</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">9%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">MA Standard Deduction (Single)</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">$4,400</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">MA Avg Property Tax Rate</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">~1.23%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">MA State Sales Tax</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">6.25%</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">Massachusetts Tax Calculator FAQ</h2><div class=\"space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How much is Massachusetts state income tax in 2026?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Massachusetts has a flat 5% rate on most income, plus a 4% surtax (the millionaire&#x27;s tax) on income exceeding $1 million — making the effective top rate 9%. For the vast majority of earners making under $1M, it&#x27;s just 5%. That&#x27;s lower than many progressive states&#x27; top rates but higher than flat-tax states like Pennsylvania (3.07%) or Indiana (3.05%).</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does Massachusetts have a standard deduction?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Nope. Massachusetts doesn&#x27;t offer a standard deduction or personal exemption at the state level. Your entire gross income (minus any pre-tax deductions like 401(k) or HSA) is subject to the 5% rate. That&#x27;s a drawback compared to states like Georgia or North Carolina that offer standard deductions.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">What is the Massachusetts millionaire&#x27;s tax?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Voters approved a 4% surtax on income above $1 million starting in 2023, bringing the effective rate to 9% on that portion. So if you earn $1.2M, the first $1M is taxed at 5% ($50,000) and the next $200K is taxed at 9% ($18,000). It only affects roughly 1% of Massachusetts taxpayers but generates significant revenue for education and transportation.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does Massachusetts tax Social Security benefits?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">No. Massachusetts does not tax Social Security benefits. However, most other retirement income — including 401(k) withdrawals, IRA distributions, and pensions — IS taxed at the 5% flat rate. That makes Massachusetts less retiree-friendly than states like Florida or Texas that have no income tax at all.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How does the overall tax burden in Massachusetts compare?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Massachusetts has a moderate-to-high overall tax burden. The 5% flat income tax is reasonable, but property taxes average 1.15%, the combined sales tax is 6.25% (state only — no local sales tax), and there&#x27;s no standard deduction. On a $75K salary, you&#x27;d pay about $3,750 in state income tax, which is more than Indiana ($2,220 after exemptions) but less than California (around $4,100).</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Is Massachusetts tax-friendly for retirees?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Not particularly. While Social Security is exempt, pensions, 401(k), and IRA withdrawals are all taxed at 5%. Property taxes are above average at 1.15%, and the cost of living in Massachusetts — especially housing near Boston — is among the highest in the country. Florida or New Hampshire (no income tax on wages) are better options for retirees in the region.</div></details></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Articles</p><div class=\"grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"><a class=\"group rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-all\" href=\"/blog/florida-vs-texas-tax-comparison\"><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors mb-1\">Florida vs Texas Tax Comparison</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed line-clamp-2\">A detailed comparison of the tax structures in Florida and Texas — two of the most popular no-income-tax states for relocation.</p></a><a class=\"group rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-all\" href=\"/blog/2026-federal-tax-brackets-explained\"><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors mb-1\">2026 Tax Brackets: IRS Income Tax Brackets 2026 Explained</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed line-clamp-2\">Complete guide to the IRS 2026 tax brackets — income tax brackets 2026, marginal tax rate, federal income tax rates, adjusted gross income, and tax credits for married couples filing jointly.</p></a></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Calculators</p><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Paycheck Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/new-york-tax-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>New York Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/relocation-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Relocation Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/self-employment-tax-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Self-Employment Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/salary\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Salary After Tax</a></div></section><div class=\"mt-8\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 mb-3\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link2 lucide-link-2 h-4 w-4 text-emerald-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M9 17H7A5 5 0 0 1 7 7h2\"></path><path d=\"M15 7h2a5 5 0 1 1 0 10h-2\"></path><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line></svg><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground\">Link to This Calculator</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">Help others find this free tool — add a link to your website or blog.</p><div class=\"space-y-2\"><label class=\"text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground\">HTML Link Code</label><div class=\"relative\"><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-muted/30 border border-border/20 p-3 text-xs text-foreground/80 font-mono\">&lt;a href=&quot;https://thetaxcalc.com/massachusetts-tax-calculator&quot; title=&quot;Massachusetts Tax Calculator 2026 | 5% Flat &amp; 9% Surtax&quot;&gt;Massachusetts Tax Calculator 2026 | 5% Flat &amp; 9% Surtax&lt;/a&gt;</pre><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground dark:hover:bg-accent/50 rounded-md gap-1.5 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 absolute top-1.5 right-1.5 h-7 px-2 text-xs\" aria-label=\"Copy link code\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-3 w-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg></button></div></div><button class=\"mt-3 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-3 w-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Show<!-- --> embed code for your website<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-3 w-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></s