"💰\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Salary After Tax\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Take-home pay at every level\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"25:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12 space-y-10\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How This Calculator Works\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Massachusetts charges a flat 5% income tax rate, with a 9% surtax on income over $1,000,000. For most earners, it's a straightforward 5% — no brackets to figure out. The state standard deduction is $4,400 (single) or $8,800 (married). On a $100,000 salary after the standard deduction, you'd pay about $4,780 in state tax. Simple enough.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"The 9% surtax kicks in on taxable income above $1,000,000, making the effective top marginal rate 9% on that excess income. If you're earning seven figures in Massachusetts, that surtax is significant — it turns a $1.5M income into roughly $70,000 more in state tax compared to someone just under the threshold.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"On top of state tax, you've got federal progressive brackets with the standard deduction, plus FICA at 7.65% combined. \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/401k-retirement-calculator\\\\\\\"\\u003e401(k) contributions\\u003c/a\\u003e reduce taxable income at both the federal and state level, which is especially valuable here since Massachusetts doesn't allow many other state-level deductions.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Massachusetts doesn't tax Social Security benefits. Property taxes average about 1.23%, and the combined sales tax is 6.25% — one of the lower state sales tax rates. No local sales tax add-ons either. \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/relocation-calculator\\\\\\\"\\u003eCompare MA to other states\\u003c/a\\u003e to see if the tax picture works for you.\\\"}}]]}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How It's Calculated\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Formula\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"MA State Tax = (Gross Income − MA Standard Deduction) × 5%, plus 9% surtax on income over $1M\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Step-by-Step\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ol\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"l