-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"Calculate your 2026 Massachusetts take-home pay after 5% flat state tax (9% surtax over $1M), federal tax & FICA. No sign-up.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Last reviewed: January 2026 · Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T & state revenue departments\"}]]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"$L27\",null,{\"componentKey\":\"massachusetts\"}]\n23:[\"$\",\"$L28\",null,{\"calculatorType\":\"massachusetts\",\"calculatorSlug\":\"massachusetts-tax-calculator\"}]\n24:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-8 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3\",\"children\":\"Related Tools & Resources\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/paycheck-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/paycheck-calculator\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"💵\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Paycheck Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Full take-home pay breakdown\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/new-york-tax-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/new-york-tax-calculator\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"🏠\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"New York Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Compare NY 4%–10.9% vs MA 5%/9%\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/relocation-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/relocation-calculator\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"📊\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Relocation Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Compare MA to other states\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/salary\",{\"href\":\"/salary\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"💰\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Salary After Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Take-home pay at every level\"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 space-y-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"How This Calculator Works\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Massachusetts charges a flat 5% income tax rate, with a 9% surtax on income over $1,000,000. For most earners, it's a straightforward 5% — no brackets to figure out. The state standard deduction is $4,400 (single) or $8,800 (married). On a $100,000 salary after the standard deduction, you'd pay about $4,780 in state tax. Simple enough.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The 9% surtax kicks in on taxable income above $1,000,000, making the effective top marginal rate 9% on that excess income. If you're earning seven figures in Massachusetts, that surtax is significant — it turns a $1.5M income into roughly $70,000 more in state tax compared to someone just under the threshold.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"On top of state tax, you've got federal progressive brackets with the standard deduction, plus FICA at 7.65% combined. <a href=\\\"/401k-retirement-calculator\\\">401(k) contributions</a> reduce taxable income at both the federal and state level, which is especially valuable here since Massachusetts doesn't allow many other state-level deductions.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Massachusetts doesn't tax Social Security benefits. Property taxes average about 1.23%, and the combined sales tax is 6.25% — one of the lower state sales tax rates. No local sales tax add-ons either. <a href=\\\"/relocation-calculator\\\">Compare MA to other states</a> to see if the tax picture works for you.\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"How It's Calculated\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"Formula\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"MA State Tax = (Gross Income − MA Standard Deduction) × 5%, plus 9% surtax on income over $1M\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"Step-by-Step\"}],[\"$\",\"o